// `Wrapped?` is Optional<Wrapped>; a Wrapped value is promoted where an
// optional is expected. In a switch arm's condition,
// `optional.present(let value)` binds the payload of the present case, and
// `optional.present` alone narrows a stable optional (a let, a parameter, a
// #reflection value, or a member path of one) to that payload for the rest
// of the condition's `&` chain and the arm's body.
@optional
enum Optional<Wrapped> {
    case absent
    case present(Wrapped)
}
